Loreweaver 3.0 is written in TypeScript and runs on Bun. This product includes
software and design derived from the following projects:

- EJS (Apache License 2.0)
  A minified copy is vendored (assets/vendor/ejs.min.js) and embedded in the
  server, which renders SillyTavern-style lore templates with it inside a
  room's worker thread. License text: assets/vendor/EJS-LICENSE.

- Lodash (MIT License, Copyright OpenJS Foundation and other contributors)
  A minified copy is vendored (assets/vendor/lodash.min.js) and offered to
  those templates as `_`. License text: assets/vendor/LODASH-LICENSE.

- SealDice (sealdice-core, MIT License)
  The Chinese command words, the Call of Cthulhu success-level ladder, the
  house-rule table and the skill-alias tables are re-implemented here, as
  rule-pack data and command tables, based on SealDice's design.

- avrae/d20 (MIT License)
  The dice notation follows d20's grammar. The dice engine is this project's
  own; none of d20's code is used.

- SillyTavern (AGPL-3.0)
  Loreweaver reads SillyTavern character cards and lorebooks so that existing
  content can be played. The code that imports them, activates lore entries
  and substitutes macros (server/src/core/worldbook/, server/src/core/card/)
  is this project's own TypeScript, written to behave as SillyTavern does and
  with reference to its source (public/scripts/world-info.js, macros.js,
  variables.js), whose function names its comments cite.

Versions 2.x were written in Python and vendored a trimmed platform-adapter
and gateway layer from hermes-agent (MIT License, Copyright 2025 Nous
Research); 3.0 contains none of that code.

Other dependencies are installed from the npm registry under their own
licenses (see bun.lock and each package's license file).

Game content:

- This product includes material from the System Reference Document 5.1 ("SRD
  5.1") by Wizards of the Coast LLC, available under the Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International License (CC-BY-4.0):
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

- Call of Cthulhu content is limited to open / Miskatonic Repository-permitted
  material. No Chaosium copyrighted text is distributed with this repository.

No copyrighted adventure/module text is distributed with this project; users
supply their own modules at runtime.
